  "summary": "As a Software Engineer at Fidelity Investments, I apply my skills in Python, Java, and C to develop and maintain high-quality financial software solutions for various clients and stakeholders. I work with a team of talented and experienced engineers, analysts, and managers to deliver innovative and reliable products that meet the needs and expectations of the market. I have been working at Fidelity since Jun 2022, and I have contributed to multiple projects, such as enhancing the security and performance of the online trading platform, improving the user interface and functionality of the mobile app, and integrating new data sources and APIs. I have a Bachelor of Engineering in Computer Science at Virginia Tech, where I have learned and practiced the fundamentals and advanced concepts of software engineering, data structures, algorithms, databases, networks, and operating systems. I am passionate about learning new technologies and applying them to solve real-world problems. I am also interested in exploring the applications and implications of artificial intelligence, machine learning, and blockchain in the financial sector. My goal is to become a proficient and versatile software engineer who can create value and impact for both the company and the society.",
